  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chefland is a city that always changes. It can be viewed as a grid with a fixed width NNN (with NNN columns numbered 111 through NNN) and changing height. The rows of the grid are numbered with positive integers. Each cell in Chefland has a colour, which is either '0' or '1'.\n\nFrom a cell (x,y)(x, y)(x,y), it is possible to move to one of the cells (x+1,y−1)(x+1, y-1)(x+1,y−1), (x+1,y)(x+1, y)(x+1,y) and (x+1,y+1)(x+1, y+1)(x+1,y+1), but only if the destination cell exists and has the same colour as the origin cell.\n\nIn Chefland, rows sometimes appear or disappear. However, a row may only appear at the bottom of the grid or disappear if it was at the top of the grid; whenever that happens, rows are renumbered with positive integers from top to bottom in such a way that the topmost row has number 111.\n\nNow, Chef received a difficult task ― keeping track of the number of ways to move from the topmost row to the bottommost row. He is asking you to help him answer QQQ queries. Initially, the grid is empty ― it has 000 rows. There are three types of queries:\n\n\n`add L`: You are given a string LLL with length NNN. A new row appears; for each valid iii, the colour of the cell in this row and the iii-th column is LiL_iLi​.\n`remove`: The topmost row disappears.\n`path c d`: Find the number of paths starting in the cell in the topmost row and ccc-th column and ending in the cell in the bottommost row and ddd-th column. Two paths are considered different if there is a cell which is visited in one path, but not in the other. Since this number can be very big, compute it modulo 1,000,000,0071,000,000,0071,000,000,007.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤201 \\le N \\le 201≤N≤20",
      "1≤Q≤300,0001 \\le Q \\le 300,0001≤Q≤300,000",
      "∣L∣=N|L| = N∣L∣=N",
      "LLL contains only characters '0' and '1'",
      "1≤c,d≤N1 \\le c, d \\le N1≤c,d≤N",
      "for each `path` or `remove` query, the grid is not empty",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):**",
      "N≤10N \\le 10N≤10",
      "Q≤300Q \\le 300Q≤300",
      "**Subtask #2 (30 points):**",
      "N≤10N \\le 10N≤10",
      "Q≤30,000Q \\le 30,000Q≤30,000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ.\nEach of the following QQQ lines describes a query in the format described above.",
    "outputFormat": "For each `path` query, print a single line containing one integer ― the number of paths modulo 1,000,000,0071,000,000,0071,000,000,007.",
    "notes": [],
